Ladybird tries an absolute-start or sticky RegExp at its only eligible
position before considering a whole-input literal search. V8’s and
SpiderMonkey’s Compiler::PreprocessRegExp() omit the search prefix for
sticky patterns and patterns anchored at the start. JavaScriptCore’s
YarrPatternConstructor::optimizeBOL() marks start-anchored
alternatives for a single pass.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 agreed on matches
and lastIndex across multiline, sticky, global, case-insensitive,
Unicode, lookahead and alternative patterns. On ordinary template
text, anchored prefix misses took the same order of time at
10,000 and 200,000 code units.
